1985

Open model inference API, web search, Linux sandboxes and agents behind
one key. OpenAI Responses, OpenAI Chat Completions and Anthropic Messages
compatible. No signup form, no prompts stored. Pay per token with a card
or a USDC wallet. https://1985.sh

Models

  Kimi K3, GLM 5.3, GLM 5.3 Flash, Qwen 3.8 Max, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash,
  MiniMax M3, GPT OSS 120B, Nemotron 3.5 Lightning
  Prices per million tokens: https://1985.sh/models

Get a key

  ssh 1985.sh key                    free key, your SSH key is your identity
  https://1985.sh/plans              monthly plans by card
  https://1985.sh/docs/pay           per token from a USDC wallet, x402

Use any OpenAI or Anthropic SDK

  Code written for OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter, Fireworks, Together or
  Groq works by changing the base URL to https://api.1985.sh/v1

  curl https://api.1985.sh/v1/responses \
    -H "authorization: Bearer $KEY" \
    -d '{"model":"kimi-k3","input":"hello"}'

  from openai import OpenAI
  client = OpenAI(base_url="https://api.1985.sh/v1", api_key=KEY)

Endpoints

  /v1/responses           OpenAI Responses
  /v1/chat/completions    OpenAI Chat Completions
  /v1/messages            Anthropic Messages
  /v1/models              models and prices
  /v1/search              web search with page text
  /v1/sandboxes           Linux sandboxes for running code
  /v1/agents              give a goal, get a result
  https://mcp.1985.sh     MCP server for agents

Command line

  curl 1985.sh | sh                  macOS, Linux
  irm 1985.sh | iex                  Windows
  brew install 1985-sh/tap/1985      Homebrew
  cargo install nineteen85           Rust

  1985 run kimi-k3 "hello"
  1985 models
  1985 search "query"
  1985 sandbox new | exec <id> <command> | rm <id>
  1985 agent "goal"
  1985 key free

SDKs

  pip install 1985                   Python, import nineteen85
  npm install @1985-sh/sdk           TypeScript and JavaScript

  Both are single files with no dependencies.

Verify

Each release at https://dl.1985.sh/v<version>/ has SHA256SUMS and
SHA256SUMS.sig. The installers check both. To check by hand:

  echo "release@1985.sh ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAINGqKKKJUla6KqHWFdiZ96h1gRLZZJIkRZOxEW9JuyiF" > allowed_signers
  ssh-keygen -Y verify -f allowed_signers -I release@1985.sh -n 1985 -s SHA256SUMS.sig < SHA256SUMS

macOS binaries are signed and notarized with Apple team ZVNS4T4UVP.
Windows binaries are Authenticode signed. Linux binaries, and macOS
and Windows binaries before signing, are reproducible from the tagged
source with rustc 1.101.0-nightly (19833af72 2026-10-20).

